  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Office of the Economic Adviser, Ministry of Commerce &amp; Industry (DPIIT). "Index Numbers of Wholesale Price in India: April 2026." Press release, 14 May 2026 (provisional). Major-group, group, sub-group and item indices retrieved via the eSankhyiki API, vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>.</p>
        <p>The headline is computed by India Atlas from the three major-group indices using the official weights (Primary 22.62, Fuel &amp; power 13.15, Manufactured 64.23); it tracks the published headline within 0.10 pt across the decade. The food index is published directly by the OEA and is shown as published.</p>
        <p>Coverage below the majors is complete: all 29 two-digit groups, all 134 sub-groups and all 697 items: major-group → group → sub-group → item, the finest grain the OEA publishes. Item weights are not served by the API, so no weighted recomposition is asserted at that level; every year-on-year figure on this page is computed by India Atlas from the published index levels, never taken from the release's growth columns.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions &amp; uncertainty</h6>
        <p>WPI is released provisional and finalised roughly eight weeks later: unlike the CPI, which is final on release. Where the source restates a figure, the previous vintage is archived, not overwritten.</p>
        <p>Where something is not measured, this guide says "we do not know" rather than inventing a number.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Prices, version 1.2, April 2026 print: adds the 697-item extremes ledger, the item cross-section CSV and three item rows in the register. Next scheduled revision: mid-June 2026, on release of the May print.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
